<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launch window background, and nothing else.

  This is the one colour the platform needs before any Compose code runs, so it cannot
  come from the generated token objects. It is therefore the single place where a hex
  value is duplicated out of design-canon/tokens.json by hand — kept honest by naming the
  token it mirrors. If `bg` changes, change this too.

  The four colours that used to live here (black_nothing, surface_nothing,
  text_main_nothing, text_muted_nothing) were prototype leftovers. Nothing referenced
  them and none of their values matched tokens.json, so they were deleted rather than
  corrected: a resource that disagrees with the canon is worse than no resource.

  Qualified by night, because the OS theme is all that is known at launch. The in-app
  theme override is read from disk one frame later.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- mirrors tokens.json `bg`.light -->
    <color name="launch_background">#F5F5F5</color>
</resources>
